/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The loop has five parts.
   - Open loop means the ECU uses tables only, with no oxygen feedback.
   - Mono-point EFI uses one injector mounted above the throttle plate in a throttle body.
   - Fuel pressure is low, about 1 bar above manifold pressure, and the injector pulses in step with the crank signal, usually once for every cylinder firing, so each pulse serves whichever cylinder is drawing in.
   - Multi-point EFI (MPFI) has one injector per cylinder, mounted in the intake port just upstream of the inlet valve.
   - Firing can be simultaneous, batch or sequential.
   - Compared with mono-point, MPFI gives better distribution, faster response and lower wall wetting.
   - The ECU first estimates the air mass that enters one cylinder in one cycle, from the air-flow meter or from manifold pressure, speed and air temperature.
   - tinj = mair ÷ (A/F × qs) + tdead mair is the air per cylinder per cycle (g); qs is the static injector flow (g/s); tdead is the opening delay (s).
*/
