/* book exam traps: Mono-point does not mean one injector per cylinder. It means one injector in total, at the throttle body; multi-point has one per cylinder at the ports. | Pulse width sets fuel mass only because pressure is held constant. If the pressure regulator fails, the same pulse width gives a different fuel mass. | Closed loop needs a hot oxygen sensor. A cold engine runs open loop, so the ECU ignores the oxygen signal during warm-up. | Sequential injection needs cylinder identification from a camshaft sensor; batch and simultaneous firing can run from the crank sensor alone. | Forgetting the dead time. The pulse is the fuel time plus the opening delay; and one four-stroke cycle is two revolutions, not one. */
