/* book: lead: Gasoline direct injection (GDI) sprays petrol straight into the combustion chamber instead of into the inlet port. The fuel arrives after the air is trapped, so the ECU decides not only how much fuel each cylinder gets but also where in the chamber it goes and at what crank angle. That lets the engine cool its charge, resist knock, raise its compression ratio and, at light load, burn a lean layere */
