/* book Worked example 2: Q: In stratified mode at 2000 rpm a cylinder needs 12 mg of petrol. At the chosen rail pressure the injector delivers 10 mg per millisecond. The injection must end 35° before TDC. How long is the injector open, how many crank degrees does that take, and when must it start?
   1. Open time = 12 ÷ 10 = 1.2 ms.
   2. Crank angle = 6Nt = 6 × 2000 × 0.0012 = 14.4°.
   3. Start = 35° + 14.4° = 49.4° before TDC.
   Answer: 1.2 ms, 14.4° of crank, starting about 49° before TDC. The fuel then has only about 35° (2.9 ms) to form the cloud before TDC, which is why the spray must be fine and the pressure high. */
