/* book exam traps: GDI is not port injection with a different name: the injector is in the chamber, the pressure is tens to hundreds of bar, and injection timing is a free choice. | Stratified does not mean the whole charge is rich. The cloud at the plug is rich enough to ignite; the cylinder as a whole is lean. | Writing that GDI keeps the inlet valves clean. It is the opposite: port injection washes the valves, GDI does not, so valve deposits are a GDI problem. | The charge-cooling estimate uses A/F to get fuel per kg of air; dividing hfg by cp alone gives an impossible 300 K drop. | A three-way catalyst cannot remove NOx from lean stratified exhaust; that is why stratified engines need a lean NOx trap. */
